==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*kweþaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*gʷet-}} (compare {{etyl|cel-pro|-}} {{m|cel-pro|*bet-lo-||mouth}} in {{etyl|sga|-}} {{m|sga|bél}}). Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{m|ofs|qwetha}}, {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|quethan}}, {{m|osx|queþan}}, {{etyl|odt|-}} {{m|odt|quethan}} ({{etyl|dum|-}} {{m|dum|quedden}}), {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|quedan}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|kveða}} ({{etyl|is|-}} {{m|is|kveða}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|kvæde}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|kväda}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌵𐌹𐌸𐌰𐌽}}.

